"Prejudgment Claim of Right to Possession | California Courts | Self Help Guide (https://selfhelp.courts.ca.gov/jcc-form/CP10.5)\nciteturn1632search0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: yesterday; # Prejudgment Claim of Right to Possession (CP10.5) ... It gives the person a chance to add themselves to the eviction court case at the beginning to say why they shouldn’t be evicted.\n\n# Prejudgment Claim of Right to Possession (CP10.5)\n\nGiven by a landlord to a person they’re trying to evict when they don’t know their name. It gives the person a chance to add themselves to the eviction court case at the beginning to say why they shouldn’t be evicted.\n\nGet form CP10.5\n\nEffective: June 15, 2015--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nStatutory Forms | Judicial Branch of California (https://courts.ca.gov/forms-rules/court-forms/statutory-forms)\nciteturn1632search1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; ## Court Forms ... CP10  | 2015  | Claim of Right to Possession and Notice of Hearing ... For more information on how to fill out forms, please visit the section \"How to fill out court forms.\"\n\n# Statutory Forms\n\n[Input]\n\n## Court Forms\n\n  * Using Forms\n  * Latest Changes\n  * Statutory Forms\n  * Appellate Claim Form\n\nThe forms below are provided for by the Legislature in statutes and are made available by the Judicial Council. Please refer to each form to locate the relevant statute for more information. \n\nForm  | Year  | Description\n--- | --- | ---\nCP10  | 2015  | Claim of Right to Possession and Notice of Hearing\nCP10.5  | 2015  | Prejudgment Claim of Right to Possession\nBOF 1022  | 2026  | Prohibited Persons Relinquishment Form (rev. 01/26)\nBOF 1022 S  | 2024  | Prohibited Persons Relinquishment Form (rev. 7/24) (Spanish)\nBOF 1023  | 2026  | Prohibited Person Firearm Information (rev. 01/26)\nBOF 1024  | 2024  | Designee Firearm Relinquishment Information\nBOF 1025  | 2024  | Firearm Disposition Receipt (rev. 7/24)